    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I put a Bitcoin or USDT wallet address on an invoice?</summary>
      <p>Yes. The payment section lets you add any number of wallets, each with a coin label and an address. Addresses print as selectable text so your client can copy them from the PDF. You can also issue the invoice itself in BTC, ETH, USDT, USDC, SOL or XMR.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Does it calculate VAT or sales tax?</summary>
      <p>It calculates tax at one rate across the whole invoice or per line item, and supports prices that already include tax. You choose the label, such as VAT, GST or Sales tax. It does not know your local rules, so check the requirements that apply to you.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I make invoices in Arabic or Persian?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Document labels are available in English, Spanish, French, German, Portuguese, Arabic and Persian, with right-to-left layout for Arabic and Persian. The text you type stays exactly as you wrote it.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Does Invoice Studio email invoices or send payment reminders?</summary>
      <p>No. It creates the document and saves it as a PDF through your browser's print dialog. You send the PDF yourself. That is the trade-off for keeping everything on your own device.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Can I use it on Windows, Mac, Linux or a Chromebook?</summary>
      <p>Yes. Invoice Studio is a single HTML file that runs in a modern desktop browser such as Chrome, Edge, Firefox or Safari. There is nothing to install.</p>
    </details>
    <details class="faq">
      <summary>Is this a subscription?</summary>
